| `check_D` private imports | Refuses an absolute import of another package's `_private` module, `from pkg import _sub`, and imported attribute chains such as `pkg._sub` from outside `pkg/`, so `__init__.py` stays the API. Numeric floor parts fully match `[0-9]{1,4}`; invalid parts exit CONFIG. | `make check` | — | Attribute chains resolve import bindings, including aliases and dotted imports; shadowing locals and parameters, private attributes without a submodule on disk, and a package's own access are allowed. It also flags the stdlib `_thread` and `_pytest` internals, and has no waiver. A `.py` file no check can parse is an error; under an interpreter older than `layers.backend.python`'s floor it is one warning per run instead, because there newer syntax cannot be told from a broken file. Package presence and allowed versions for core requirements, configured extras and enabled transport extras are judged by `scripts/check_venv.py`. | [limits-and-troubleshooting.md](../guides/limits-and-troubleshooting.md) | always |
